## Testing requirements (do not skip)

1. **Schema validation tests**: unknown field rejected; operator/field-type
   mismatch rejected; incomplete `between` rejected; empty `in`/`not_in`
   rejected; duplicate `rule_id` on create rejected; a well-formed rule
   passes with zero errors.
2. **Translator tests**: a composite AND/OR condition produces the
   expected SQL shape and correctly ordered parameters.
3. **Dry-run tests**: match count against a known sample dataset matches
   a manually computed expected count; every previewed row actually
   satisfies the condition; switching AND→OR on the same leaf conditions
   never decreases the match count.
4. **Store tests**: create → update (version increments, prior version
   backed up) → soft-delete (status flips, file retained) → audit log
   contains one entry per mutation in the right order.
5. If building the UI in a browser-based environment where headless
   browser automation isn't available, at minimum extract and
   unit-test the pure validation/translation/dry-run logic directly
   (no DOM dependency) so correctness is verified even without a full
   click-through test.

